{"task": "IG-2B08", "path": "docs/work/WORKFLOW.md", "start_line": 81, "lines": ["depending on children, while children inherit the parent's former dependencies (never", "depend on the parent). Rewire downstream tasks through parent closure. Validate the DAG,", "check target-set coverage without overlaps, and render child cards. No recursive platform", "or agent manager is needed. Work partitions do not reduce the full-rulebook target.", "", "## Checkpoints, interruption and conflicts", "", "Write `private/workflow/runs/<task>/<attempt>/checkpoint.json` before starting and after", "each usable increment: task/attempt, actor, actual config, base file hashes, changed-file", "hashes, input packet hash, completed criteria, command results, blocker and next operation.", "Freeze a delivery manifest of all reviewed files and record reports in the same run folder.", "Do not overwrite prior attempts. A interrupted task remains in_progress until triaged.", "Resume by comparing checkpoint hashes with disk and the current queue; record divergences,", "retain both versions and resolve only owned files. Never reset, clean or stash the worktree.", "If an unexpected writer changed an owned path, block that path and ask the coordinator", "to integrate. A checkpoint is not a commit and never authorizes push.", "", "At most two repair cycles per review finding and two retries for the same unchanged", "failure. Then block with evidence and the smallest decision needed. A new hypothesis", "or changed external condition must be recorded before another attempt. No silent scope", "expansion or weakened tests to clear a blocker.", "", "## Measurements and report", "", "Record start/end UTC, elapsed wall time, executor/reviewer identities, requested and", "observed configuration, token counts only if exposed, operator time only if reported,", "tests and defect counts by severity. Unknown values are null, not zero. Separate code", "quality from source meaning and full-profile readiness. No invented monetary cost.", "Final handoff includes outcome, paths/hashes, criteria met/unmet, commands and exits,", "independent review, human decisions where needed, remaining risks, and next exact action.", "", "## Permissions and context limitations", "", "Packets enforce their own allowlist and reject history paths, path escapes and symlinks.", "They are not an OS sandbox for arbitrary tools. `.rgignore` controls default ripgrep only;", "explicit paths, `--no-ignore`, other tools and Git can bypass search exclusions.", "Read [archive isolation](../ARCHIVES.md) before any historical access. The current session", "cannot migrate outside its writable roots or install under protected `.agents/`."], "truncated": false}

